# ZWarden remote Agent — environment template (F35, ADR 0038).
#
# Copy to `.env` (or run ./bootstrap-env.sh) and fill in the values. `.env` is git-ignored — the enrollment
# secret is a one-time credential and must never be committed. Compose reads it automatically.
#
# Unlike the control-plane stack, a remote Agent holds NO key ring and NO database, so there are no secrets to
# generate here — only the domain to reach and the one-time enrollment secret the control plane hands you.

# --- Required: the control-plane hostname ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The public DNS name of the ZWarden control plane this Agent connects to (the SAME ZWARDEN_DOMAIN the control
# plane serves), e.g. zwarden.example.com. The Agent dials wss://<domain>/agent/hub outbound over the Internet.
ZWARDEN_DOMAIN=

# --- Required for first enrol: the one-time enrollment secret (F9) --------------------------------------
# On the control plane, sign in and open Enroll (First-Run wizard, or Hosts → enroll). It issues a single-use,
# short-lived enrollment secret. Paste it here, then `docker compose up -d`. The Agent enrols once and persists
# its own per-Agent credential on the agent_state volume — you can blank this again afterwards.
ZWARDEN_ENROLLMENT_SECRET=

# --- Project Zomboid runtime (F13/F14) ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pinned canonical PZ image this Agent provisions servers from — a repo@sha256:… DIGEST (a floating tag
# like :latest is rejected, ADR 0008). May be left blank until you provision your first server on this host.
ZWARDEN_PZ_IMAGE=
# The Docker network provisioned PZ containers attach to on this host (default: zwarden-pz).
ZWARDEN_PZ_NETWORK=zwarden-pz
